  Quote of the Week:

  Elizabeth I, Queen of England, to her subjects in 1601:
  "You have had, and may have, many mightier and wiser princes sitting upon 
this throne; yet you never had, nor shall have any that will love you 
better."


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:

  In spring, Bradipo I has been informed by Uga-Buga Makumb (#1) that his 
cooperation has become unnecessary, and therefore our formerly amicable 
relations are now broken.

  With the coming of the spring season, Bradipo I prepared to quench his 
thirst for glory.  Orielle was hit by a plague.  The plague struck the 225th 
Skeletal Legion in Orielle and destroyed them.  Bradipo I levied the 251st 
Eagles in Kiska to serve Bradipo I.
  Windy spring blossomed into early summer.  Bradipo I practiced his 
Necromancy well but could not improve his skill in Necromancy.

  A conquering horde owing their allegiance to 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0) invaded the province of Orielle, a 
Plain area ruled by Bradipo I.  Tlazolteotl (#88)'s armies took control of 
Orielle practically uncontested.  Tlazolteotl leads approximately 3 Phalanx 
and 3 Dragons.
  Midsummer's night came and went and late summer came.  Bradipo I's 
Skeletal Army spell fizzled and Bradipo I wound up with his face covered 
with psycho-kinetic slime.

  Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0)'s minions initiated a campaign of 
conquest in Kiska, a Mountain province owing allegiance to Bradipo I.  Alain 
(#33) was in command of the attacking armies.  The defenders were commanded 
by Bradipo I.  The armies were drawn up into lines of battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Kiska (0207):

