  DEFENDING ARMY

  The attackers had the 304th Dragons, the 335th Dragons, the 309th Legion, 
the 291st Trolls and the 189th Skeletal Bowmen in reserve.  Alain commanded 
a host of loyal soldiers.  Bradipo I marched with his loyal troops, eyes set 
in terrible resolution.
  The Skeletal Armies led by Babba Sissoko (#0) marched into battle with a 
fanatical fervor.  Alain (#33) stepped forward and challenged Bradipo I to 
personal combat.  Bradipo I refused to enter personal combat.
  The forces commanded by Bradipo I were dismayed by his cowardice.  They 
marched on, though with shaken confidence.  As luck would have it, some 
bandits raided his supply elements, giving Alain the edge.  As the battle 
developed, the tactical abilities of Bradipo I and Alain appeared evenly 
matched.

  Across the entire front, the Veteran 137th Skeletal Phalanx faced the 
Veteran 265th Axemen, who were joined by a troop of the Order of Knights 
Hospitaller, who exhorted them to fanaticism with their Good and vaunted 
fury.  The 126th Skeletal Dragons soared over the 141st Eagles and attacked 
them.  The 271st Dragons swooped down on the 251st Eagles and attacked them. 
The 304th Dragons swooped down on the 265th Axemen and attacked without 
mercy.  The 141st Eagles swooped down on the 126th Skeletal Dragons and 
attacked without mercy.  The 251st Eagles soared over the 271st Dragons and 
attacked them.  The 137th Skeletal Phalanx fought the 265th Axemen and 
crushed their skulls as if they were eggplants.
  Alain's armies shattered the army opposing them with a final charge.  The 
137th Skeletal Phalanx slew the 265th Axemen almost to a man.  The 126th 
Skeletal Dragons scattered the 141st Eagles in all directions.  The 271st 
Dragons destroyed the 251st Eagles.
  Alain's well-planned campaign accomplished the conquest of Kiska.  His 
forces completely destroyed, Bradipo I escaped alone to Abu Matariq.  His 
efforts improved his skill in Tactics.
  With the coming of the fall season Bradipo I attempted an illegal move.  
He tried to move from Abu Matariq to Khalturin, a non-adjacent province.  
Instead, Bradipo I rode into Kiska.

  An army coming from the empire of Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0) 
invaded Abu Matariq, hoping to subjugate that province ruled by Bradipo I 
and made up of great Deserts.  Alain (#33)'s forces conquered Abu Matariq 
without any major engagements.  Alain leads approximately 1 Bowmen, 1 
Phalanx, 1 Legion, 4 Dragons and 1 Trolls.
  With the advent of the early winter season instead of practicing, 
Bradipo I tried to complete his previously ordered movement.  He journeyed 
to Khalturin.


  A host of warriors carried the banner of Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango 
(#0) into the Jungle province of Macondo, ruled by Bradipo I.  Macondo was 
overrun by Alain (#33)'s host.  Alain leads approximately 1 Bowmen, 1 
Phalanx, 1 Legion, 4 Dragons and 1 Trolls.
  Thus endeth the adventures of Bradipo I for this year.


  Bradipo I treated with his ally Cosmic Herderer Mugai (#3).  Bradipo I 
treated with his ally Hokuto (#4).  Bradipo I treated with his ally Prometeo 
(#5).  Bradipo I treated with his ally II Kahn (#6).  Bradipo I treated with 
his ally Giovanna (#7).  Bradipo I treated with his ally Circe (#8).  
Bradipo I treated with his ally Agesilao (#9).

  Here is the financial report for Bradipo I's kingdom: this turn, the 
Kingdom collected 0 gold in revenue.  2 gold was expended to finance our 
leaders.  0 gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Bradipo I was left 
with 105 gold in the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Adele
To: Bradipo I

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I travelled to Big Sky.
  The wet spring was followed by early summer.  I rode into Mongu.
  With the coming of the late summer season, I really tried hard to improve 
my Element Magic, but I practiced in vain.
  During fall, Adele's Tornado spell backfired and I was left covered with 
psycho-kinetic slime.  A strange magical counterspell seemed to have impeded 
my spell.
  The fall season darkened into early winter.  I tried a Skeletal Army 
spell, but botched it.

  Thy humble servant,   Adele


From: Indra
To: Bradipo I

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season, I prepared to quench my thirst for 
glory.  I tried to practice my Sageness, but the task seemed beyond my 
aptitude.  My efforts raised my aptitude in Sageness.  I discovered nothing 
worthy of note in my sagely researches.
  Windy spring was followed by early summer.  Rainulf (#25) tried a Kill 
Enemy spell, but bungled it.  In my sagely researches, I discovered a 
fabulous invention called the Pepper Spice!  The following benefits are 
conferred by the Pepper Spice:
  Congratulations, you have discovered the Pepper Corn!  All you have to do 
is grind up those little suckers, sell the spice at jacked-up Royal Monopoly 
prices and you will increase your Kingdom's revenue by an average of 3% each 
gameturn.

  In late summer, I invented nothing valuable in my sagely researches.
  The sultry days of summer surrendered to the fall.  I invented nothing 
valuable in my sagely experiments.
  With the coming of the early winter season Indra's Clairvoyance spell 
backfired and I was left with my face covered with psycho-kinetic slime.  A 
strange magical aura may have impeded my spell.

  Thy humble servant,   Indra


